Minimization changes the order of the variables to implicitly change to a new
Noether normalization, but doesn't actually recompute the integral closure
presentation as a strict affine algebra over the new Noether normalization.
Therefore a second call to an integral closure method is required if the output
of normalization doesn't suffice. It does produce the three outputs needed as
input to either qthIntegralClosure or rationalIntegralClosure. I don't
necessarily like this second call. At the current time it is easier to use the
output of minimization to produce manually (as above) a good minimization.

Ways to use minimization:
=========================

  * "minimization(List,List,Ring,Matrix)"

