This is just like qthIntegralClosure except over QQ instead of ZZ/q. It calls
qthIntegralClosure for several small primes q and reconciles the results using
the Chinese Remainder Theorem and the extended Euclidean algorithm.

See also
========

  * *note icFractions: (IntegralClosure)icFractions, -- fractions integral over
    an affine domain
  * *note integralClosure: (IntegralClosure)integralClosure, -- integral
    closure of an ideal or a domain

